          "summary": "Add an SFJ performance warranty (professional and workmanlike, Protocol/SOP/GCP/Applicable Laws) with a re-performance remedy at SFJ's cost in § 13.5.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] SFJ's only substantive warranty is that it will have sufficient funds, yet SFJ sponsors and conducts the Clinical Trials in the SFJ Territory, so we have added a performance warranty for the activities SFJ actually performs plus a re-performance remedy at SFJ's cost. This tracks our playbook position that the party performing the work stands behind it to a professional standard; the existing Article 13 carve-out in § 13.6.2 preserves it against the disclaimer.",
          "ops": [
            {
              "kind": "replace",
              "paragraphId": "p0739",
              "oldText": "13.5 SFJ Representation, Warranty and Covenant. SFJ hereby represents, warrants and covenants that it will have, as and when needed, sufficient funds to satisfy its obligations hereunder.",
              "newText": "13.5 SFJ Representations, Warranties and Covenants. SFJ hereby represents, warrants and covenants that (a) it will have, as and when needed, sufficient funds to satisfy its obligations hereunder; and (b) all Clinical Trials activities and other obligations performed by SFJ or any Permitted Third Party utilized by SFJ hereunder will be performed in a professional and workmanlike manner by suitably qualified personnel, consistent with industry standards and in accordance with the applicable Protocol, the SFJ SOPs, GCP and all Applicable Laws. In the event of any breach of the warranty in clause (b), SFJ will, at PB's request, promptly re-perform or otherwise correct the affected activities at SFJ's sole cost and expense, and the costs of such re-performance or correction will not be included in Development Costs or credited against SFJ's funding obligations hereunder. The foregoing remedy is in addition to, and does not limit, any other remedy available to PB under this Agreement."
            }
          ]
